#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:5 1ded8c466bb14b5187a6712ea47b6296
msgid "Crash Check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:7 80b34b7dc1ac4425bcdcb9400ab6d8a2
msgid ""
"Copter includes a crash check which disarms the motors in cases where the"
" vehicle is likely out of control and has hit the ground.  This reduces "
"damage to the vehicle and also reduces the chance of injury to people "
"near the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:9 b2c31750003c4e4c8281cb8281ff093e
msgid ""
"The crash check is similar to the :ref:`parachute release <common-"
"parachute>` logic except that the parachute will normally release as the "
"vehicle falls, while the crash check should trigger once the vehicle has "
"hit the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:12 605bbbed92974f158520ff0b4c5de020
msgid "When will the crash check disarm the motors?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:13 3a98cd5ce63240e6b227df592f74e82d
msgid "When all the following are true for 2 full seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:15 ba0422fde03d42d4bf14d3c058d51454
msgid "the vehicle is armed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:16 c2618aaa14cf451193ac200a131fe60e
msgid "the vehicle is not landed (as far as it can tell)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:17 b83c05ccaf8c4038a4a2198afe8137d7
msgid "the current flight mode is *not* ACRO or FLIP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:18 dd12904f4b084d68964fce8b02099248
msgid "the vehicle is not accelerating by more than 3m/s/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:19 c78cb9b84e944a0dac40e58b81898a59
msgid ""
"the actual lean angle has diverged from the desired lean angle (perhaps "
"input by the pilot) by more than 30 degrees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:22 33a9e2fcbb5d4a2f9f4689b97d873929
msgid "What will happen when the crash check fires?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:24 4e5ac8eba27f48ccb87f8d4e4d24c186
msgid "the motors will disarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:25 29a06d49c13a4b16a9686e521c2a7579
msgid "\"Crash: Disarming\" will be displayed on the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:26 24c2a936244046f494fb1a0c6f9a46f1
msgid ""
"a crash event will be written to the dataflash logs (look for EV, 12 in "
"the logs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:29 50f0e6ae600445068c60a2fe00991c23
msgid "How and when should the crash check be disabled?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:30 bbb9e14d79214dddbbf482a40f023260
msgid ""
"In general the crash check should be left enabled but if the vehicle is "
"likely to suffer from lean angle errors of over 30 degrees for a second "
"or more it should be disabled.  This includes applications where the "
"vehicle is being used to carry a guide wire from one mountain peak to "
"another or being used for \"drone boarding\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:35 82cc83fa1a2641389e8c223304dccf65
msgid ""
"Image courtesy of `The Verge <https://www.theverge.com/2016/2/3/10905970"
"/droneboarding-is-happening>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/crash_check.rst:37 176f1e79318e47e685b142d6b5108da3
msgid ""
"In Copter-3.3.3 (and higher) the crash check can be disabled by setting "
":ref:`FS_CRASH_CHECK <FS_CRASH_CHECK>` to 0."
msgstr ""

